quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  112,1,"Say: ‘He is Allah, the Unique One."
  112,2,Allah is Self-Sufficient and the Most Superior Sustainer upon whom all depend.
  112,3,He neither begets nor was He begotten (i.e. He is neither a father nor a son).
  112,4,And none is equal (or comparable) to Him.’
  113,1,"Say: ‘I seek refuge in the Lord Who brought the universe into existence with an explosion (or: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak),"
  113,2,"against the harm of whatever He has created,"
  113,3,"and against the harm of the night when it becomes utterly dark,"
  113,4,"and against the harm of those (witches) blowing on knots,"
  113,5,and against the harm of the envious when he envies.’
  114,1,"Say: ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of humankind,"
  114,2,"the Supreme Sovereign of humankind,"
  114,3,"the God of humankind,"
  114,4,"from the evil of the whisperings of the sneaky (Satan),"
  114,5,"who whispers into the breasts of humans,"
  114,6,from among the jinn and humans.’
